horizon forbidden west is the  long-awaited sequel to horizon zero dawn  and throws ailoy into a beautiful but  dying world full of powerful machines as  she tries to discover why the world is  ending the game gives you a lot of  tricks up your sleeve to stop the  apocalypse again so here are nine things  i wish i knew before playing horizon  forbidden west  it might not feel like it but it has  been five whole years since horizon zero  dawn launched for playstation 4. if you  don't know your elizabeth sobek from  your ted farrow or remember exactly what  gaia and her subordinate functions did i  definitely recommend checking out a  recap before you boot up horizon  forbidden west the game takes place six  months after the events of zero dawn and  while it has a brief video explainer at  the start it's really in your best  interest to watch a recap if you haven't  played zero dawn recently trust me on  this luckily for you we made a great one  right here on gamespot that you can  check out after you've finished this  video  horizon forbidden west comes with a  great suite of options and accessibility  features to tweak and i really recommend  looking through the menus because some  of the options are incredibly useful  horizon is a beautiful game that  encourages exploration so i'd recommend  playing in explorer mode and changing  your hud to be dynamic that way there's  less on-screen hud clutter to improve  your immersion in a fight horizon can  throw a lot at you and different enemies  will have different weaknesses to give  yourself a little advantage change your  weapon wheel slowdown to slower that way  you can swap ammo types and weapons with  ease with less risk of getting run over  by a charging machine and i'm speaking  from experience because that happened to  me all the time if you find yourself in  the middle of the desert without an  overridden mount to ride to your next  location you might get a bit fed up with  needing to push in the thumb stick to  make aloy sprint you can set her to auto  sprint both on foot and when on a mount  which is very useful for traversing big  distances just don't forget to turn it  off if you're undertaking a platforming  section because otherwise you might miss  that pixel perfect jump  [Music]  horizon forbidden west has six huge  skill trees compared to zero dawn's four  allowing you to spec aloy in a way  that's more closely in line with how you  want to play the game the skill trees  can be overwhelming at first but because  upgrade points come in pretty thick and  fast it's in your best interest to  experiment leveling up and completing  missions including side content gives  you a couple of points per activity and  early skill tree abilities including  active skills and passive buffs are  relatively cheap a couple that i'd  recommend getting early on are silent  strike heel from the infiltrator tree to  gain back health when you use a silent  strike it's super useful if you're  taking out a fortress and you run out of  healing items in the survivor tree  invest in potent medicine to improve the  speed and amount of health you get from  medicinal berries and grab plant forager  as fast as you can aloy needs to do a  lot of ammo crafting so this comes in  clutch if you're big into laying traps  for your enemies definitely prioritize  that skill tree not only can you lay and  make traps quicker but you can take less  damage if you accidentally set off one  of your own  new to forbidden west are valor surges  powerful unlockable abilities that can  really give you the edge in a fight  think of them as aloy's ultimates you  can unlock a few and swap them on the  fly but as you can invest more points to  upgrade the abilities and make them  stronger here are some good ones to  prioritize in the infiltrator tree  stealth stalker allows you to  temporarily activate a cloaking device  in the middle of battle be aware that  you won't go completely invisible but  it's enough to help you lose some heat  at higher levels you get a damage boost  against unaware enemies and if you kill  them while cloaked you can prolong your  cloaking for longer also in the  infiltrator tree is radial blast which  acts as a knockback if you find yourself  completely surrounded by enemies firing  this off sends out a shock wave that  damages everyone around you and it's  extremely useful in a pinch  [Music]  if you take anything away from this  video i hope it's this the traps you lay  are op  when i played zero dawn i think i only  laid the ones in the tutorial and never  really bothered again in forbidden west  i was fully ready to commit to my bow  lifestyle again and look i fully admit  that when possible i am a stealth archer  but when i came up against a really  tough boss and was completely out of the  ammo type that carried its elemental  weakness i remembered that i had that  ammo in abundance in trap form those  traps decimated that boss's health bar  and fully built up the elemental bar too  meaning that it started to take extra  damage over time  now i stealth around battle arenas and  carefully lay traps everywhere there's  no greater joy than watching a machine  fall into your perfectly laid trap what  was that  aloy's focus is incredibly useful and  while you'll mostly use it to ping the  environment to find collectibles items  and handholds to climb you should be  using it at the start of every fight the  game tries to encourage you to do this  at the start but it's very easy to  forget but let me tell you the forbidden  west has a bunch of new machines to come  up against and it's in your best  interest to scan each and every one for  weaknesses when scanning with your focus  hit the touchpad to pause time  completely to read all the strengths and  weaknesses information way more easily  it tells you whether you're able to use  the machinist amount as well as giving  you a rundown of all the possible loot  you can get from it including valuable  information about how to get it off the  creature  this is definitely worth taking note of  as some resources get destroyed if you  don't detach them from the machine's  body before killing it plus some parts  drop weapons that you can use against  the machines you're fighting against so  make sure to hide in the bushes and scan  scan scan  don't get attached to one weapon  throughout the course of forbidden west  you'll find a truckload either through  the story or by buying them from the  many merchants you'll come across while  you can upgrade them at the workbench  honestly i would save those resources  and upgrade later in the game because at  the start you'll quickly get better  weapons anyway if you want to upgrade  anything at the start of the game you  should prioritize your pouches by  hunting organic animals that way you can  carry more weapons and ammo it's  important to make sure that every  elemental weakness is covered though so  you don't come up short against certain  machines and to help you out on the  battlefield make sure you have weapon  quick swap turned on in the menus  tapping l1 mid fight will swap to either  your last used weapon or a particular  one that you've predetermined in the  weapon wheel  across the course of the game aloy will  scavenge and pick up many many items and  while a lot can be used for crafting  some are just marked automatically as  valuables to sell instead of mass  selling those whenever you get to a  merchant make sure you're not actually  hanging on to something that could have  another use some machine hearts are used  for upgrades and other items can be used  to buy machine parts from salvage  contractor merchants  make sure it says that the item is only  used for selling for metal shards before  selling something you might regret  you might be tempted to mainline the  story but there's a lot of great side  content and character moments you'll  miss out on if you do the side quests  are really fun and well written and feel  fresher than the ones from zero dawn  there are also collectibles and relic  ruins which are climbing puzzles that  reminded me a lot of the ones from  assassin's creed ii  even unlocking the tall nexus one  requiring you to work a little harder to  reach the top of the giant creatures  when you get there though you get to  unlock the map and the shock wave it  emits kills all the surrounding machines  which gives you a little xp boost and  items to loot and you get to glide off  the top of it which i'd argue is the  biggest reward  so there's some starter tips for horizon  forbidden west but if you're looking for  help with combat our very own max  blumenthal is putting together his best  combat tips for you so make sure you  like this video and subscribe to  gamespot so you don't miss it i'm on  twitter at lucy james games thanks for  watching  [Music]  you
 

